/ herb:slots client
/ herb:state (position: "bottom-right")
.min-h-full.bg-white data-controller="toasts"
  .mx-auto.max-w-4xl.px-4.py-6
    header.mb-6.flex.items-baseline.justify-between
      h1.text-2xl.font-bold Toasts
      p.hidden.text-sm.text-gray-500.sm:block one stack, fed from JavaScript or straight from the server
    p.mb-8.text-sm.text-gray-500
      ' The toaster is a single
      code.rounded.bg-gray-100.px-1 &lt;ol data-moly-toaster&gt;
      | , at the bottom
        of this page so the corner can be state driven. In a real application it belongs in the layout.
        A behavior measures each toast, stacks them, runs the timers and handles the swipe. Everything you see is CSS
        driven by the custom properties it writes, so the page owns the look.
        Hover the stack to expand it and pause every timer, drag a toast toward the nearest edge to dismiss it, or press Escape.
    section.mb-10
      h2.mb-1.text-sm.font-semibold.text-gray-900 From JavaScript
      p.mb-4.text-sm.text-gray-500
        code.rounded.bg-gray-100.px-1 toast()
        |  is imperative and works from anywhere. These buttons go
          through a five line Stimulus controller.
      .flex.flex-wrap.gap-2
        - [ \
            ["plain", "Message"],
            ["success", "Success"],
            ["error", "Error"],
            ["warning", "Warning"],
            ["info", "Info"],
            ["describe", "With a description"],
            ["undo", "With an action"],
            ["promise", "Promise"],
            ["sticky", "Stays until closed"],
            ["many", "Five in a row"],
          ].each do |action, label|
          button> type="button" data-action="toasts##{action}" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 transition hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50" = label
        button type="button" data-action="toasts#dismiss" class="rounded-lg border border-transparent px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-gray-400 transition hover:text-gray-700"
          | Dismiss all
    section.mb-10
      h2.mb-1.text-sm.font-semibold.text-gray-900 From a Rails flash
      p.mb-4.text-sm.text-gray-500
        ' These post, set
        code.rounded.bg-gray-100.px-1 flash
        '  and redirect. The layout renders the flash
          as list items inside the toaster, and the behavior adopts them on connect with timers and swipe intact. No
          JavaScript is involved, and
        code.rounded.bg-gray-100.px-1 notice
        '  and
        code.rounded.bg-gray-100.px-1 alert
        |  land as success and error.
      .flex.flex-wrap.gap-2
        - ToastsController::KINDS.each_key do |kind|
          => button_to kind.capitalize, "/toasts/notify", params: { kind: kind }, class: "rounded-lg border border-gray-200 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 transition hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50"
    section.mb-10
      h2.mb-1.text-sm.font-semibold.text-gray-900 Where it sits
      p.mb-4.text-sm.text-gray-500
        ' The corner is the value of the attribute the behavior is registered on, and here it comes from
        code.rounded.bg-gray-100.px-1 herb:state
        | . Changing it re-places the whole stack, because the
          behavior is handed the new value and the stylesheet anchors off the same attribute.
      .flex.flex-wrap.gap-2
        - %w[top-left top-center top-right bottom-left bottom-center bottom-right].each do |corner|
          button> herb-key="#{corner}" type="button" data-herb-set=="position='#{corner}'" class="rounded-lg border px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium transition #{position == corner ? "border-lime-600 bg-lime-50 text-lime-700" : "border-gray-200 text-gray-700 hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50"}" = corner
    section.mb-10
      h2.mb-1.text-sm.font-semibold.text-gray-900 What the behavior writes
      p.mb-4.text-sm.text-gray-500
        | Nothing here is styled by the package. Each toast carries its place in the stack, the distance it should sit
          from the anchored edge and its collapsed scale, and the stylesheet turns those into a translate.
      .overflow-x-auto.rounded-xl.border.border-gray-200
        table.w-full.text-left.text-sm
          thead.bg-gray-50.text-xs.uppercase.tracking-wide.text-gray-500
            tr
              th.px-4.py-2.font-medium Property
              th.px-4.py-2.font-medium Holds
          tbody.divide-y.divide-gray-100
            - [ \
                ["--moly-toast-index", "its place in the stack, 0 at the front"],
                ["--moly-toast-y", "how far it sits from the anchored edge, already signed"],
                ["--moly-toast-scale", "the collapsed scale, 1 once expanded"],
                ["--moly-toast-swipe-x", "the live swipe offset"],
                ["--moly-toaster-front-height", "the front toast's measured height"],
                ["--moly-toaster-gap", "the gap between toasts"],
              ].each do |name, holds|
              tr
                td.px-4.py-2.font-mono.text-xs.text-gray-900 = name
                td.px-4.py-2.text-gray-500 = holds
    p.text-sm.text-gray-500
      ' The same package ships the
      a href="/drawers" class="font-medium text-lime-700 hover:underline" drawer
      ' , and
        both are registered by one
      code.rounded.bg-gray-100.px-1 install()
      |  call against the Herb runtime.
  ol data-moly-toaster="#{position}"
    - flash.each do |kind, message|
      li data-moly-toast="#{kind}": div(data-moly-toast-content): div(data-moly-toast-title) = message
